senses.gloss:
प्रखर प्र-खर, अस्, आ, अम्, very hot or
acrid, acrid, biting, pungent; very hard or rough;
(अस्), m. iron armour for the defence of a horse or
elephant [cf. प्रक्खर, प्र-क्षर]; a mule;
a dog.

प्र-खिदत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, Ved. thrusting away;
harassing, afflicting (according to Mahī-dhara = प्र-
कर्षेण खेदयत्).
